  "rules": [
    "Persist the full local checkpoint inventory before the first source case; seal only after every source was registered",
    "A case contains one old Run and one old source binding/attempt; a new model or Run does not rewrite it",
    "Hash the exact original manifest using Python-compatible json-sort-keys-compact-utf8-v1, without adding defaults",
    "Hash evidence canonicalPayloadUTF8 bytes directly; decoding body never grants executor permission",
    "ACK is a monotonic historical fact and uses ackKey; it carries planRevision rather than expectedRevision and no current branchFence",
    "apply accepts only immutable server actionIds and requires current planId/expectedRevision/source hash/branchFence plus Idempotency-Key",
    "Partial ACK does not settle other required action kinds, including equal API evidence hashes",
    "After registration, prompt/API dispatch requires the full current inventory/generation/control fence; legacy unregistered branches retain v1 behavior",
    "A cancelled recovery keeps receipts and unresolved effects; historical ACK cannot revive it",
    "transportGoal defaults to ready; released requires an explicit release_idle_transport permission; none requests only reconciliation",
    "Native state=outcome_unknown cannot be changed into rejected by a completed HTTP error receipt",
    "Terminal continuation is unsupported in Gate88; no SDK/model/tool business replay is performed",
    "For api_attempt ACK replace sourceSessionId with sourceAttemptId and retain the same sourceRun/checkpoint/store identity",
    "API complete/terminalKnown is a provider-attempt outcome, not task success or a host tool execution permit",
    "An API attempt missing its original bodySha256 is legacy evidence_unavailable; unknown/partial outcomes do not authorize paid retry",
    "Native transport planning closes admission until the required transport action has a durable native step proof; it does not alternate ready/release goals",
    "Only an original managed API contract-1 request may use the API admission fence; it does not protect legacy proxy requests",
    "GET API lookup 404 is not a not-sent proof. POST reconcile atomically observes the existing attempt or fences a truly absent/prepared managed key",
    "A proven managed API admission fence creates an api_attempt source with resolve_source_checkpoint only; it never dispatches to a provider",
    "A proven transport-only sdk_writer_busy or local capacity_exceeded refusal can receive a fresh native action ID; the old step receipt remains unchanged",
    "A local policy rejection before native dispatch is a transport-only rejected_not_sent step; current permission checks run before the step becomes started"
  ],
